{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BFVKipzrYFYa45io9UHagj","type":"tool_result","content":"275\t# not catch it because that test moves the component AND adds an SR, and the SR\n276\t# is the only reason its finding exists.\n277\t#\n278\t# Two independent blind spots, both closed here: the frame REGISTRIES were not\n279\t# walked at all, and the cell set was `Status` only, while the derivation also\n280\t# reads a CMP's `Standing` (a lifecycle fact that holds rung 3 on its own), an\n281\t# SR's `SN-Refs` (the coverage rung) and `Verification` (the LLR exemption), and\n282\t# the child rows' parent refs (the decomposition rungs). A rule that reads a\n283\t# narrower input set than the derivation it polices can always be walked past.\n284\t#\n285\t# The BEFORE side already carried these rows — `_spine_at` materializes the\n286\t# whole declared input set at `rev` — so this is an attribution fix, not a new\n287\t# read.\n288\t_ATTRIBUTED_ROWS = (\n289\t    (\"SR-ID\", \"srs\", (\"Status\", \"SN-Refs\", \"Verification\")),\n290\t    (\"LLR-ID\", \"llrs\", (\"Status\", \"SR-Refs\")),\n291\t    (\"TC-ID\", \"tcs\", (\"Status\", \"Verifies\")),\n292\t    (\"B-ID\", \"bifs\", (\"Status\",)),\n293\t    (\"CMP-ID\", \"cmps\", (\"Status\", \"Standing\")),\n294\t)\n295\t\n296\t# The two of those that carry no `Phase` cell. The boundary and partition rungs\n297\t# are REPO-GLOBAL — which is precisely how they drop every phase at once — so a\n298\t# decrease attributed to one of them cannot be answered by tagging a phase, and\n299\t# its finding says so rather than asking for something the row cannot carry.\n300\t_PHASELESS_KEYS = frozenset({\"bifs\", \"cmps\"})\n301\t\n302\t# THE EXEMPTION, and it is exactly one permutation (owner answer §6.2): a\n303\t# decrease landing precisely on DevStg-LLReqs -> DevStg-Arch is the PERMITTED\n304\t# DECOMPOSITION CYCLE — architecture rework surfaced by breaking a requirement\n305\t# down is within-phase churn, and any deeply decomposed problem would otherwise\n306\t# run the phase counter up. The owner declined a wider Arch-tier exemption, so\n307\t# this is a pair, not a predicate over the Arch rung: a two-rung drop that\n308\t# happens to END at Arch is NOT exempt, and neither is Arch -> anything.\n309\t_EXEMPT_DECREASE = (kitladder.STAGE_LLREQS, kitladder.STAGE_ARCH)\n310\t\n311\t\n312\tdef _spine_at(root, rev):\n313\t    \"\"\"`load_spine` over the DECLARED INPUTS as they stood at `rev`, or None when\n314\t    git cannot answer — the kit's silent-no-op degrade, not an error.\n315\t\n316\t    THE INPUTS ARE MATERIALIZED INTO A TEMP TREE AND THE LIVE LOADER IS RUN OVER\n317\t    IT, rather than parsing each `git show` into rows here. Three things come\n318\t    free that a re-implementation would have to get right and could drift on:\n319\t    carrier resolution (`.toml` before `.csv`, and `.md` for needs), the `-000`\n320\t    example filter, and — the one that actually bites — the `have_bifs`/\n321\t    `have_cmps` applies-when, where an ABSENT registry and an EMPTY one mean\n322\t    opposite things at the two inserted rungs. Materializing only the files that\n323\t    existed at `rev` preserves absence as a value.\n324\t\n325\t    THE WHOLE FRAME IS READ AT `rev`, NOT HELD AT THE LIVE TREE. Holding it\n326\t    constant was tried first and is wrong: the ruled exemption is\n327\t    `DevStg-LLReqs -> DevStg-Arch`, and the Arch rung is derived from the\n328\t    COMPONENT registry, so a frame pinned to the live tree makes the owner's one\n329\t    permitted decrease unreachable — the rule would be unable to see the very\n330\t    transition it is required to forgive.\"\"\"\n331\t    if _git(root, [\"rev-parse\", \"--verify\", \"--quiet\", rev]) is None:\n332\t        return None  # no git, or no such revision: nothing to compare against\n333\t    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n334\t        found = False\n335\t        for declared, suffixes in kitstage.DECLARED_INPUTS:\n336\t            for suffix in suffixes:\n337\t                text = _git(root, [\"show\", \"{}:{}{}\".format(rev, declared, suffix)])\n338\t                if text is None:\n339\t                    continue\n340\t                dest = Path(tmp) / (declared + suffix)\n341\t                dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n342\t                dest.write_text(text, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\")\n343\t                found = True\n344\t                break\n345\t        if not found:\n346\t            return None\n347\t        return spine_rules.load_spine(Path(tmp) / \"docs\")\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tdef _by_id(spine):\n351\t    \"\"\"`{spine-key: {id: row}}` — the before-side lookup `_changed_rows` joins on.\"\"\"\n352\t    return {\n353\t        key: {r[id_col]: r for r in spine.get(key, []) if r.get(id_col)}\n354\t        for id_col, key, _cells in _ATTRIBUTED_ROWS\n355\t    }\n356\t\n357\t\n358\tdef _effective(spine):\n359\t    \"\"\"The headline value for a spine dict — the settled, per-phase, floored fold,\n360\t    i.e. exactly what `derive()` puts in the `stage` field.\n361\t\n362\t    THE TEST-EVIDENCE VERDICT IS DELIBERATELY LEFT AT ITS DEFAULT (False) HERE,\n363\t    on BOTH sides of the phase rule's before/after comparison (WI-500). The rule\n364\t    polices SPINE AUTHORING — an edit that lowers the reading must surface as a\n365\t    phase change — and evidence is not an authored row: a suite that went red, or\n366\t    a record that went stale, would otherwise read as an un-phased authoring\n367\t    decrease and demand a phase tag nobody can supply. Symmetric omission keeps\n368\t    the comparison about the rows, which is what the rule is for.\"\"\"\n369\t    _live, settled_per_phase = _stage_map(spine, settled=True)\n370\t    return kitstage.effective_stage(settled_per_phase)[0]\n371\t\n372\t\n373\tdef _changed_rows(live, before_rows):\n374\t    \"\"\"Every row this edit ADDED, or whose STAGE-AFFECTING CELLS it moved, as\n375\t    `[(id, key, row, before-status-or-None)]` over `_ATTRIBUTED_ROWS`.\n376\t\n377\t    THE TRIGGER SET IS WIDER THAN THE PLAN'S WORDS, and the measurement is why.\n378\t    Plan §4 says \"a newly drafted/redrafted row\"; driven on a frame-free spine\n379\t    (slice 3), a newly DRAFTED row cannot decrease the effective stage AT ALL —\n380\t    slice 1 excludes drafts from the settled fold, so that half of the phrase is\n381\t    inert by construction. What actually decreases it is a redrafted child\n382\t    (Impl -> LLReqs for an LLR, Impl -> Tests for a TC) and a newly APPROVED\n383\t    parent with no children yet (Impl -> LLReqs). Narrowing to the literal words\n384\t    would have shipped a rule that cannot fire on the two shapes that matter, so\n385\t    the trigger is \"added, or a stage-affecting cell moved\" — which CONTAINS the\n386\t    plan's set.\n387\t\n388\t    IT IS THE DERIVATION'S CELLS, not `Status` alone — see `_ATTRIBUTED_ROWS`\n389\t    for what was walked past while this compared one cell in three registries.\"\"\"\n390\t    out = []\n391\t    for id_col, key, cells in _ATTRIBUTED_ROWS:\n392\t        prior = before_rows.get(key, {})\n393\t        for row in live.get(key, []):\n394\t            rid = row.get(id_col)\n395\t            if not rid:\n396\t                continue\n397\t            was = prior.get(rid)\n398\t            if was is None:\n399\t                out.append((rid, key, row, None))\n400\t                continue\n401\t            moved = [\n402\t                \"{} {} -> {}\".format(\n403\t                    c,\n404\t                    (was.get(c) or \"\").strip() or \"(blank)\",\n405\t                    (row.get(c) or \"\").strip() or \"(blank)\",\n406\t                )\n407\t                for c in cells\n408\t                if (was.get(c) or \"\").strip().lower()\n409\t                != (row.get(c) or \"\").strip().lower()\n410\t            ]\n411\t            if moved:\n412\t                out.append((rid, key, row, \"; \".join(moved)))\n413\t    return out\n414\t\n415\t\n416\tdef phase_rule_findings(root):\n417\t    \"\"\"The authoring-time decrease rule (plan §4, owner answer §6.1).\n418\t\n419\t    **An edit that LOWERS the effective stage must surface as a phase change.**\n420\t    When the effective stage decreased, every row this edit added or moved a\n421\t    stage-affecting cell on must carry a `Phase` tag that is NOT the phase the\n422\t    settled work was standing in — a NEW (higher) phase, or an already-open\n423\t    LOWER one. Both readings of \"the scope moved\" satisfy it; quietly adding\n424\t    regressing work to the phase you are standing in does not.\n425\t\n426\t    THE ATTRIBUTED SET IS EVERY STAGE-AFFECTING INPUT, not the spine tiers\n427\t    alone (`_ATTRIBUTED_ROWS`, widened at the WI-498 close). A frame row has no\n428\t    phase to tag, so its finding reports the decrease and names the cause\n429\t    instead of demanding a cell the row cannot carry.\n430\t\n431\t    WHY THIS SHAPE AND NOT A STORED COUNTER (plan §4, alternative (ii) rejected):\n432\t    phase stays a pure function of the registries. The derived `phase=` still\n433\t    increments BECAUSE the rows say so, so there is no second phase concept to\n434\t    drift against the row tags, and `docs/stage` records the derived value\n435\t    exactly as `docs/gate` did.\n436\t\n437\t    WARN TIER, AND THE ARMING PATH IS THE POINT. This returns findings; `main`\n438\t    prints them and exits 0 unless `--strict`. New rules arm warn-first here\n439\t    unless a ruling says otherwise, and OI-51's ruling establishes that the rule\n440\t    EXISTS, not that it hard-fails on day one. It promotes by being wired into\n441\t    `check.py`'s `--strict` trio at a threshold — deliberately NOT done in this\n442\t    slice, because a rule whose fire has never been observed on real authoring\n443\t    should not be able to block a commit. The promotion is one call-site edit:\n444\t    the predicate and its vocabulary do not change (`trace.schema_advisories`'s\n445\t    warn-first twin idiom).\n446\t\n447\t    DEGRADES SILENTLY WITHOUT GIT, like every other two-tree rule in the kit: no\n448\t    HEAD means no before-state, and a rule that cannot see the past has nothing\n449\t    to say rather than something to complain about.\n450\t\n451\t    Implements: SR-181\n452\t\n453\t    RE-POINTED AT WI-501 (OI-53 (b), 2026-08-22). This carried\n454\t    `Implements: SR-139` until the WI-498 close, which was a mis-trace: SR-139\n455\t    is \"Approval as an ordinal over a derived spine stage\" — it governs the\n456\t    `human_approval_through` dial — while this rule's obligation is \"a\n457\t    spine edit that LOWERS the effective stage must surface as a phase change\"\n458\t    (ruled plan §4, owner answer §6.1). Unrelated obligations at different\n459\t    tiers, so `backlink-coverage` was crediting a requ
[... byte cap hit — full stream in out/run-logs/ ...]
 that lowers the effective stage while its row carries the phase the settled spine already stood in is a finding naming the row, the drop and the cause; the SAME edit re-tagged into a NEW higher phase produces nothing, and re-tagged into an ALREADY-OPEN LOWER phase also produces nothing - both readings of a moved scope are asserted, not just the forward one. THE EXEMPTION IS DRIVEN AS A PAIR AND NOT AS A DESTINATION: the DevStg-LLReqs -> DevStg-Arch decrease is asserted silent, and a two-rung decrease that merely ENDS at Arch is asserted to FIRE - the arm that separates the permitted decomposition cycle from a scope regression wearing its destination. THE ATTRIBUTED SET IS DRIVEN BEYOND THE SPINE TIERS: a component-only edit and a boundary-only edit that each lower the reading are asserted to produce their findings, since a rule that walked only SR/LLR/TC would be silent on exactly the frame rows that drop every phase at once. The re-drafted-child arm is driven (a row moved back to Drafted inside the standing phase fires), and the counterpart is asserted too: a NEW Drafted row cannot lower the effective stage at all, so it is not a finding under any tag. DEGRADATION IS ASSERTED AND NOT ASSUMED: with no git repository the rule returns the empty list rather than raising or complaining. THE CLI TIER IS ASSERTED ON BOTH SIDES: `--phase-rule` prints WARN and exits 0 on a finding, and `--strict` promotes the same finding to FAIL and exit 1 - the warn-first posture the requirement states as part of the obligation. Finally the rule is driven against THIS repository's own tree and asserted clean, so the check that guards authoring is itself observed passing on the artifact it guards.\"\"\"\ntier = \"Full\"\nexpected = \"Satisfies SR-181: a registry edit that drops the derived effective stage is a finding unless every row it added or moved a stage-affecting cell on carries a phase other than the one the settled work stood in; the single DevStg-LLReqs to DevStg-Arch decrease is exempt; a frame row is reported with its cause rather than asked for a cell it has no place for; the rule is silent with no committed before-state and reports at warn tier\"\nautomated = \"Yes\"\nevidence = \"\"\"tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_committed_baseline_is_a_settled_IMPL_spine; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_lowering_edit_in_the_STANDING_phase_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_same_edit_with_a_NEW_phase_tag_PASSES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_an_ALREADY_OPEN_LOWER_phase_also_satisfies_the_rule; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_LLREQS_to_ARCH_decrease_is_EXEMPT; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_TWO_RUNG_decrease_that_merely_ENDS_at_Arch_is_NOT_exempt; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_COMPONENT_ONLY_decrease_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_BOUNDARY_ONLY_decrease_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_REDRAFTED_child_in_the_standing_phase_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_NEW_DRAFT_cannot_lower_the_effective_stage_AT_ALL; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_without_git_the_rule_has_NOTHING_TO_SAY; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_CLI_is_WARN_FIRST_and_STRICT_promotes; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_THIS_repo_does_not_fire_the_rule\"\"\"\nstatus = \"Drafted\"\nphase = 5\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2107,"oldLines":5,"newStart":2107,"newLines":5,"lines":[" expected = \"Satisfies SR-181: a registry edit that drops the derived effective stage is a finding unless every row it added or moved a stage-affecting cell on carries a phase other than the one the settled work stood in; the single DevStg-LLReqs to DevStg-Arch decrease is exempt; a frame row is reported with its cause rather than asked for a cell it has no place for; the rule is silent with no committed before-state and reports at warn tier\""," automated = \"Yes\""," evidence = \"\"\"tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_committed_baseline_is_a_settled_IMPL_spine; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_lowering_edit_in_the_STANDING_phase_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_same_edit_with_a_NEW_phase_tag_PASSES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_an_ALREADY_OPEN_LOWER_phase_also_satisfies_the_rule; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_LLREQS_to_ARCH_decrease_is_EXEMPT; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_TWO_RUNG_decrease_that_merely_ENDS_at_Arch_is_NOT_exempt; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_COMPONENT_ONLY_decrease_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_BOUNDARY_ONLY_decrease_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_REDRAFTED_child_in_the_standing_phase_FIRES; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_a_NEW_DRAFT_cannot_lower_the_effective_stage_AT_ALL; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_without_git_the_rule_has_NOTHING_TO_SAY; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_the_CLI_is_WARN_FIRST_and_STRICT_promotes; tests/test_phase_rule.py::test_THIS_repo_does_not_fire_the_rule\"\"\"","-status = \"Drafted\"","+status = \"Approved\""," phase = 5"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
